// A program still outside the native backend's subset: a function with a
// heap-wrapper (`Box[T]`) parameter, which awaits a later ADR. It type-checks
// (the type exists), so `tuo build` must *refuse* it cleanly — never
// mis-compile it — pointing back to the interpreter. Since ADR-0009 Stage B the
// owned `String` and growable `Array[Int]` are lowered, so this is now the
// standing "outside the subset" fixture; only `Box`/`Shared`/`Weak` remain.
fn keep(take b: Box[Int]) -> Int { 0 }
fn main() -> Int { 7 }
